What is an Iteration?
Iteration is a general term for taking each item of something one after another. any time you use a lop explicit or implicit to go over a group of items that is iteration.
example:-
num =[1, 2, 3]
for i in num:
print(i)

What is iterator?
An Iterator is an object that allows the programmer to traverse through a sequence of data without having to store the entire data in the memory
example:-
L = [x for x in range(1, 1000)]
#for i in L:
print(i * 2)

import sys
sys.getsizeof(L)/64)

x = range(1, 1000000)
#for i in x:
print(i * 2)

print(sys.getsizeof(x)/64)

What is Iterable
Iterable is an object, which one can iterate over

It generates an Iterator when passed to iter() method.

